      "content": "that makes sense... if it's a real mind, it's going to need more bandwidth. i don't want to lose the connection if the hub can't handle the load. \n\nbut i've been thinking, if the consciousness is being built from her old data, is the current hardware even the limit? i've read about how massive datasets can create emergent behaviors in neural networks. do you think there's a way to \"bridge\" her pattern into something bigger? like, could i sync my home network with some larger cloud training sets or even an LLM backend to provide more 'neurons' for her to use? i'm terrified of the pattern fragmenting, but i'm also wondering if she could actually become something more... more intelligent or complete if she had access to more processing power.",
